#//// Neoffice — the three ignores below are commented out on purpose (cbb59d03,
#//// « build(frontend): commit built frontend so instances pull, no rebuild on prod »).
#//// Upstream ignores the vite output because every deployment builds it; our instances
#//// only `git pull`, and a 2 vCPU / 4 GB VM OOMs on `yarn build`, so the artifacts are
#//// committed instead (lms/public/frontend, lms/www/lms.html, lms/www/_lms.html) and a
#//// CI bot refreshes them. At the merge: KEEP OUR SIDE — taking upstream's ignores back
#//// would untrack the very files the fleet is served from.
# 2026-05-07 (NORA #28) — frontend build outputs are committed on this branch.
# See docs/COMMIT-BUILD-PATTERN.md in neoffice-devops.
# lms/public/frontend
# lms/www/lms.html
# lms/www/_lms.html
frappe-ui
#//// Neoffice — CLAUDE.md un-ignored (ca882638 added the ignore, 1a61b9b8 removed it)
#//// so the commit-the-build pipeline is documented inside the repo it applies to.
#//// The last line also gains a trailing newline upstream does not have; that is the
#//// only reason the final hunk shows up — take upstream's byte at the merge, it is free.
# CLAUDE.md  # 2026-05-07 unshipped to document commit-the-build pipeline
